A||N||11||NOS3800||HPP Shootout Completed||||11||
Z||000000||NOS3800||10-11-2001||09:55 PM||||Well, the HPP shootout that my brother competed in is done and finished today. This was the COOLEST thing I have ever done! And I wasn't even in the thing, I was just watching! We arrived at Englishtown Raceway at 9am. We were told to get our cars cleaned up for the photoshoot. MOPAR MUSLE magazine was also there doing a shootout between 7 Mopars. The six Pontiacs in the shootout were as follows:<BR>est. 1969 GTO convertable (running low 13's)<BR>est. 1974 Trans Am big block(running low 13's, broke after 3rd run)<BR>est. 1989 Trans Am, 350 V8+125 shot of NOS( 12.8-12.9)<BR>est 1997 Anniv Ed Trans Am, nasty SC LT1(all over 12.0- 13.8's)<BR>1967 Firebird 400 V8 race car(12's)<BR>And L1LDV1L's Fiero SC 3800<BR>The photo shoot has Devils Fiero in front of the entire group, so it should make for some good group photos. I was so jealous this entire day! I thought mine wasn't picked because I use NOS to get my times, but the Trans Am was running a 125 shot. So I asked the editors about this and they said mine may be used in a later shootout, they didn't want two of the same style car in this shootout.<BR>Well, the day didn't start out good. Earl promised 13.2's and his first run was horrible! He spun all the way through first, ended up with a 15 something, because he let off the gas and coasted. After a few smokey burnouts, the traction problem was pretty much solved. But the ET's didn't show it. 13.5's to 13.7's. Pretty dissapointing.<BR>After lunch, which the magazine paid for( pizza and soda) things got much better!<BR> First run after the hour long lunch was a 13.3 at 100 mph. The mag guys came to me and said now he's got it working good! The very next run was a 13.27! THen a 13.27 AGAIN!They were IMPRESSED! Even the MOPAR guys had to come over and watch! Evreyone there was VERY nice and extremely interested in the car. hopefully this article will change peoples opinions of our cars!<P><P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sig_Pic,_nos3800_3.jpg"> <BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.21@102.13 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||11
Z||000001||FieroMaster88||10-11-2001||09:59 PM||||Wow!  Thats awesome!  Sounds like it was lots of fun.  I cant wait to get my car done and go race (hopefully) like that!<P>How did you go about getting your car entered for something like that anyway?<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">                  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTMike||10-11-2001||10:18 PM||||whats hpp   i have never head of it.  is it short for something?  when is the article comming out?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||10-11-2001||10:42 PM||||Mike HPP is High Performance Pontiac Magazine.<P>Nos3800, sounds like you guys had a great time. Let us know when the article comes out.||||reg||1
Z||000004||sluppy123||10-11-2001||10:42 PM||||HPP is short for High Performance Pontiac. <P>It's good to hear the Fiero Finally getting some attention from the magazines, but we need more. I'd also like to know How you and your brother went about getting involved in this. <P><P>------------------<BR>-Brian, Toolmaker<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>87' GT-Galaxy silver mettalic, Turbo Charged, Modified 2.8- 235 HP w/ 7 psi Boost, Eibach Sport springs, RSM side scoops, Mr Mikes leather, 17" Mille Miglia's. <BR>                <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1711832&a=12781563&p=54316496&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||NOS3800||10-11-2001||11:19 PM||||I posted about two months ago for anyone interested in having their car in the magazine to send their info to me and I would put all the Fieros together in one envelope and send it in. While I got ALOT of response on the list, I got zero mailed to me. But you are in luck, you can still go to <A HREF="http://www.southernpontiacnationals.com" TARGET=_blank>www.southernpontiacnationals.com</A>  and get the forms there. I think its under SHOOTOUT FORMS. BTW, we mailed ours 3 weeks ago and they called one week later! However, one of the contestants told me they jhad sent theirs in a year and a half ago, so be patient.<BR>The article is going to be in the MARCH issue. The December issue is currently on shelves now, so you should see it in 2-3 months.||||reg||1
Z||000006||NOS3800||10-11-2001||11:22 PM||||I messed up the webpage address. Go to <A HREF="http://www.southernpontiacnationals.com." TARGET=_blank>www.southernpontiacnationals.com.</A>  Its under HPP Shootout.||||reg||1
Z||000007||NOS3800||10-11-2001||11:24 PM||||DAMN I'm an IDIOT!!!<P>Its <A HREF="http://www.pontiacsouthernnationals.com" TARGET=_blank>www.pontiacsouthernnationals.com</A> <p>[This message has been edited by NOS3800 (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||lildevil||10-12-2001||08:43 PM||||We did have a great time .  I think i made a good impression on the guys that were there.  BUt talking to the editor and a few of the other participants there is a TOTAL lack of knowledge about our cars.  They didn't know  a N* or 350 would fit in the Fiero.  The reason?  Because noone has taken the time to send in the photos and small write ups. Going to PONTIAC car shows helps alot also. They saw me running at Maple Grove this year.  So if you have a show worty FAST fiero send those photos in.  The more coverage we get, the more respect we will recieve.  <P><P>------------------<BR>Earl Sessions<BR>1985 Fiero w/ 1998 Supercharged 3.8 V-6<BR>Best ET: 13.232 @ 101.24 mph<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/water3quarterthumb.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000009||Denny||10-12-2001||09:16 PM||||So Bill and/or Earl (Berl), you guys never said whether or not Earl won.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> <P>BTW, way to go, and keep pluggin' our cause! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Denny (edited 10-12-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000010||lildevil||10-12-2001||09:26 PM||||Denny,<P>it was a race exactly.  It was a comparison test. Too see how fast a Pontiac can go with certain mods. If it was a race i would have been SMASHED! the other cars were in the 12's and 11's. Mainly 400 cubic inche race cars that were all trailered in. Except the GTO but he lived 30 mins away.  I could beat him.||||reg||10
Z||000011||grgoyl86||10-12-2001||10:52 PM||||Congrats!<P>Those times are really good. Especially since I was just reading the issue of Pontiac Enthusiast that I got today, with a write-up on Chris Moore's NorthStar Fiero. It shows his best time as 13.60/103.0.<P>Way to show Fiero Pride!<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieropride.com</A> ||||reg||1
